Attempt: run one triage turn (issue #859) against a real hosted model.
Endpoint: https://text.pollinations.ai/v1 (OpenAI-compatible, model "openai-fast" = gpt-oss-20b)
Setup:    OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=... repo-triager --provider configured triage --issue 859 --apply auto
Result:   openminion setup and runtime bootstrap succeeded; the action loop then failed because
          the provider rate-limits anonymous callers to one reply per 45 s:

  openminion.modules.llm.providers.contracts.ProviderError: PROVIDER_ERROR:
  The configured model provider failed before it could return a decision
  (openai request failed with HTTP 402: Free limit reached: 1 reply every 45 seconds per IP.
   Retry after 37s, or get unlimited replies with a pollen key ...).

Reason this matters: one triage turn issues 12 model calls (see findings/measure_turn_cost.py),
which needs ~9 minutes at 1 call / 45 s. The runtime's provider retry (3 attempts) cannot span
that. A real model run needs a provider without a per-request throttle - Cortensor Portal,
OpenAI, Groq, Cerebras, or a local Ollama - which is a configuration change, not a code change.

Verified instead: the same workflow end-to-end with the scripted provider on the real runtime
(repo-triager --provider scripted demo), and the live read-only GitHub path
(tests/test_github.py::test_live_fetch_reads_public_repository).
